                <pb facs="0453" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg359"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 to No. 433.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to the
                            Earl of Kimberley.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Under instructions from the State
                    Department, I have the honor to apply to your lordship for information in
                    relation to the admission of American meat products and cattle into Great
                    Britain. Copies of all decrees bearing upon the subject issued by Her Majesty’s
                    Government since 1880, including those of all the laws in this relation, would
                    be much appreciated by my Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
